# A short [[note]]; a [[memorandum]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=John Yoo|title=War by Other Means{{...|: An Insider's Account of the War on Terror}}|publisher=Atlantic Monthly Press|isbn=9781555847630|page=42|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=cSIuURhjZgsC&pg=PA42&dq=%22leaked+memo%22&hl=&cd=5&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22leaked%20memo%22&f=false|text=According to yet another leaked '''memo''', Powell responded the next day. Powell's leaked '''memo''' conceded that al Qaeda were not POWs, and that the Taliban individually or as a group might also lose their entitlement to that status.}}
# {{lb|en|programming}} A [[record]] of partial results that can be reused later without [[recomputation]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020|author=Daniel Zingaro|title=Algorithmic Thinking: A Problem-Based Introduction|publisher=No Starch Press|isbn=9781718500808|page=86|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=eY4HEAAAQBAJ&pg=PA86&dq=%22memo%22+recursion&hl=&cd=1&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22memo%22%20recursion&f=false|text=The first is that the recursive call finds its subproblem solution in the '''memo''' and returns immediately.}}

